From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 16:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] compat: let the build say the kernel already has
 skb_mark_not_on_list

compat.h decides whether to define skb_mark_not_on_list itself purely from
LINUX_VERSION_CODE: anything older than 4.14.217 gets the compat definition,
because that is where the stable series picked the helper up.

Android vendor trees do not follow that arithmetic. mindphone's kernel calls
itself 4.14.186 but carries the backport already, so the compat definition
collides with the real one and every object in the module fails to compile:

  compat.h:847:20: error: redefinition of 'skb_mark_not_on_list'
  ../kernel-source/include/linux/skbuff.h:1348:20: note: previous definition

There is no way to detect this from the preprocessor - it is a static inline
function, not a macro - so add a knob the build can set after looking at the
kernel's own skbuff.h. Kernels that follow the upstream version arithmetic are
unaffected: nothing defines it and the condition is unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [upstream is archived; this is vendor-tree specific]
---
--- a/compat/compat.h
+++ b/compat/compat.h
@@ -843,7 +843,11 @@
 #define COMPAT_CANNOT_DEPRECIATE_BH_RCU
 #endif
 
+/* COMPAT_HAVE_SKB_MARK_NOT_ON_LIST: set by the build when the kernel's own
+ * skbuff.h already declares this, which an Android vendor tree may do at a
+ * version where upstream stable had not picked it up yet.
+ */
-#if (LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(4, 19, 10) && LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(4, 15, 0) && !defined(ISRHEL8)) || LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(4, 14, 217)
+#if ((LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(4, 19, 10) && LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(4, 15, 0) && !defined(ISRHEL8)) || LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(4, 14, 217)) && !defined(COMPAT_HAVE_SKB_MARK_NOT_ON_LIST)
 static inline void skb_mark_not_on_list(struct sk_buff *skb)
 {
 	skb->next = NULL;
